 bank money,","start":21.16,"end":26.0,"score":0.986,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-002-p02","sourceId":"b4-012-002","sourceIndex":1,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[15,37],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"repayment of which he may demand at any time either in cash or by drawing a cheque in favour of another person.","start":26.59,"end":34.76,"score":0.959,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-003-p01","sourceId":"b4-012-003","sourceIndex":2,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,10],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Primarily, the banker-customer relationship is that of debtor and creditor--","start":35.92,"end":41.84,"score":0.871,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-003-p02","sourceId":"b4-012-003","sourceIndex":2,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[10,25],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"who is which depending on whether the customer's account is in credit or is overdrawn.","start":43.08,"end":48.87,"score":0.939,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-004","sourceId":"b4-012-004","sourceIndex":3,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,22],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"But, in addition to that basically simple concept, the bank and its customer owe a large number of obligations to one another.","start":49.73,"end":58.64,"score":0.953,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-005-p01","sourceId":"b4-012-005","sourceIndex":4,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,15],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Many of these obligations can give rise to problems and complications but a bank customer,","start":60.03,"end":66.24,"score":0.982,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-005-p02","sourceId":"b4-012-005","sourceIndex":4,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[15,30],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"unlike, say, a buyer of goods, cannot complain that the law is loaded against him.","start":66.6,"end":72.63,"score":0.956,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-006","sourceId":"b4-012-006","sourceIndex":5,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,13],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"The bank must obey its customer's instructions, and not those of anyone else.","start":74.16,"end":79.14,"score":0.983,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-007-p01","sourceId":"b4-012-007","sourceIndex":6,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,9],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"When, for example, a customer first opens an account,","start":80.01,"end":83.29,"score":0.985,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-007-p02","sourceId":"b4-012-007","sourceIndex":6,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[9,25],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"he instructs the bank to debit his account only in respect of cheques drawn by himself.","start":83.79,"end":89.39,"score":0.952,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-008-p01","sourceId":"b4-012-008","sourceIndex":7,"part":1,"parts":3,"wordRange":[0,8],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"He gives the bank specimens of his signature,","start":90.84,"end":93.49,"score":0.981,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-008-p02","sourceId":"b4-012-008","sourceIndex":7,"part":2,"parts":3,"wordRange":[8,15],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"and there is a very firm rule","start":93.803,"end":95.85,"score":0.999,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-008-p03","sourceId":"b4-012-008","sourceIndex":7,"part":3,"parts":3,"wordRange":[15,40],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"that the bank has no right or authority to pay out a customer's money on a cheque on which its customer's signature has been forged.","start":96.0,"end":104.46,"score":0.962,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-009","sourceId":"b4-012-009","sourceIndex":8,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,21],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"It makes no difference that the forgery may have been a very skillful one: the bank must recognize its customer's signature.","start":105.28,"end":113.42,"score":0.919,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-010-p01","sourceId":"b4-012-010","sourceIndex":9,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,13],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"For this reason there is no risk to the customer in the practice,","start":114.42,"end":118.16,"score":0.983,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-010-p02","sourceId":"b4-012-010","sourceIndex":9,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[13,24],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"adopted by banks, of printing the customer's name on his cheques.","start":118.28,"end":122.33,"score":0.882,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-012-011","sourceId":"b4-012-011","sourceIndex":10,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,14],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"If this facilitates forgery, it is the bank which will lose, not the customer.","start":123.71,"end":129.31,"score":0.964,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]}]}
